import project.dl

to get [the Studio project storage key for] {integer:mode}:
    return (the string form of "dynlex-studio-shader-project") if (mode = 1), else (the string form of "dynlex-studio-program-project")

to get [the Studio editor for mode] {integer:mode} [in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    return the UI source editor labeled ("Shader source" if (mode = 1), else "IDE source") in (state's language)

to [report Studio storage failure] {string:detail} [in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set the text of "File status" in (state's view's instance) to "An error occurred. Check the log."
    request "log" containing (a JSON object containing [JSON text "level" is "error", JSON text "message" is ("Studio project storage: " + detail)]) for purpose 0 indexed 0 in state

to get [the Studio storage reply to] {a pointer to JSON value:payload} [in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set json to the compact JSON form of payload
    free payload
    set result to a UI call named "storage" containing json through (state's services) in (state's view)
    if result's success = false:
        report Studio storage failure (result's contents) in state
        return 0 as a pointer to JSON value
    parse (result's contents) as JSON and set parsed to it
    require condition (parsed succeeded) reporting "The storage service returned invalid JSON"
    return parsed's value

to get [the Studio project snapshot of] {a pointer to UI source project:project}:
    return a JSON object containing [JSON text "entry" is (project's entry's filename), JSON child "files" is (the UI source files of project)]

to get [valid Studio project snapshot] {a pointer to JSON value:snapshot}:
    if ((JSON field "entry" in snapshot has kind the JSON text kind) = false) or ((JSON field "files" in snapshot has kind the JSON object kind) = false):
        return false
    set files to the JSON member named "files" in snapshot
    set entry to the JSON text named "entry" in snapshot
    if files lacks JSON member named entry:
        return false
    loop index from 0 to (files's length):
        set member to the item at index in (files's members)
        if (member's value's kind != the JSON text kind) or ((a Studio source path error for (member's name)) != ""):
            return false
        if ((member's name has "lib/" at offset 0) or (member's name has "packages/" at offset 0)) or (member's name has "site/language/" at offset 0):
            return false
        loop offset from 0 to (member's name's length):
            if (the character at offset in (member's name)) = (47 as a byte):
                if files has JSON member named (the substring of (member's name) from 0 spanning offset bytes):
                    return false
    return true

to [load Studio snapshot] {a pointer to JSON value:snapshot} [in] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set project to editor's document's project
    set main to project's entry
    set entry to the JSON text named "entry" in snapshot
    set files to the JSON member named "files" in snapshot
    set profiles to a copy of JSON node (project's profiles)
    configure UI source document main named entry at (the project URI for entry under (state's language's client's root)) prefixed by (main's prefix) using profiles with files (project's files)
    load UI main source of editor in (state's view) from (the JSON text named entry in files) at (state's view's seconds) seconds
    loop index from 0 to (files's length):
        set member to the item at index in (files's members)
        if member's name != entry:
            ignore add Studio file (member's name) containing (member's value's text) to editor

to get [restore Studio project for mode] {integer:mode} [from storage in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set editor to the Studio editor for mode mode in state
    set key to the item at mode in (state's studio files' storage keys)
    set result to the Studio storage reply to (a JSON object containing [JSON text "action" is "get", JSON text "key" is key]) in state
    if result = (0 as a pointer to JSON value):
        return false
    set restored to false
    set stored to the JSON member named "value" in result
    if stored is not JSON null:
        if stored's kind = the JSON text kind:
            parse (stored's text) as JSON and set parsed to it
            if parsed succeeded:
                set restored to valid Studio project snapshot (parsed's value)
                if restored:
                    load Studio snapshot (parsed's value) in editor in state
                free parsed's value
        if restored = false:
            report Studio storage failure (the string form of "Invalid stored project") in state
    free result
    return restored

to [open saved Studio projects in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set browser to the address of (state's studio files)
    if (browser's rows = (0 as a pointer to JSON value)) or (browser's opened):
        return nothing
    set browser's opened to true
    loop mode from 0 to 2:
        store (the Studio project storage key for mode) into (browser's storage keys) at mode
        ignore restore Studio project for mode mode from storage in state
        set editor to the Studio editor for mode mode in state
        store (editor's document's project's revision) into (browser's saved revisions) at mode
    display Studio files in state

to [save changed Studio projects in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set browser to the address of (state's studio files)
    if browser's opened = false:
        return nothing
    loop mode from 0 to 2:
        set editor to the Studio editor for mode mode in state
        set project to editor's document's project
        if (the item at mode in (browser's saved revisions)) != project's revision:
            store (project's revision) into (browser's saved revisions) at mode
            set snapshot to the Studio project snapshot of project
            set payload to a JSON object containing [JSON text "action" is "set", JSON text "key" is (the item at mode in (browser's storage keys)), JSON text "value" is (the compact JSON form of snapshot)]
            free snapshot
            set result to the Studio storage reply to payload in state
            if result != (0 as a pointer to JSON value):
                free result

to [attach the Studio file browser in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set browser to the address of (state's studio files)
    set browser's expanded to a new JSON-RPC object
    set browser's rows to a new JSON-RPC array
    ignore a UI overlay in (state's view) with context (state as a pointer) handling input ((the function named "read Studio file tree $ in $") as a pointer) painting (0 as a pointer) closing (0 as a pointer)

to [close the Studio file browser in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set browser to the address of (state's studio files)
    free browser's rows
    free browser's expanded
    if browser's libraries != (0 as a pointer to JSON value):
        free browser's libraries

# Ordinary projects and individual shared examples retain independent drafts.
to get [switch Studio project for mode] {integer:mode} [to session] {string:signature} [in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set browser to the address of (state's studio files)
    if browser's opened = false:
        return false
    set key to the Studio project storage key for mode
    if signature != "":
        set key to key + "/" + signature
    if (the item at mode in (browser's storage keys)) = key:
        return false
    synchronize UI source workspace (state's language) at (state's view's seconds) seconds
    save changed Studio projects in state
    set editor to the Studio editor for mode mode in state
    set project to editor's document's project
    if (mode = 1) and (state's shader editor's source request != 0):
        ignore cancel website request (state's shader editor's source request) in state
        set state's shader editor's source request to 0
    set document to project's documents
    loop while document != (0 as a pointer to UI source document):
        if (document != project's entry) and (document's writable and document's available):
            delete Studio document document in editor in (state's view)
        set document to document's next
    set main to project's entry
    set filename to (the string form of "shader.dl") if (mode = 1), else (the string form of "main.dl")
    configure UI source document main named filename at (the project URI for filename under (state's language's client's root)) prefixed by (main's prefix) using (a copy of JSON node (project's profiles)) with files (project's files)
    load UI main source of editor in (state's view) from (the string form of (editor's node's content)) at (state's view's seconds) seconds
    store key into (browser's storage keys) at mode
    set restored to restore Studio project for mode mode from storage in state
    store (project's revision) into (browser's saved revisions) at mode
    return restored
